<%--
Password_Confirmation_Form - "confirm it's you", ready to embed

The form a sensitive action asks for first: the account's password (with Turnstile), or one of
its passkeys. It is an <Rsx_Form> posting to the framework's own endpoint
(Rsx_Password_Confirmation_Controller::verify), so a host names no endpoint and writes no
verification code.

    <Password_Confirmation_Form $sid="confirm" />

What it shows follows what the account can confirm with (options() from the server):
    a password                  the password field and its submit
    a passkey (and a browser    "Use a passkey instead" - the browser's passkey prompt
    that can run one)
    neither                     a notice that this account has no way to confirm here

EVENTS
    'confirmed'  the confirmation was given (by password or passkey).
                 Rsx_Password_Confirmation.is_confirmed() is now true on this page.

METHODS
    submit()     submit the password; resolves true when confirmed, false on a refusal
                 (whose message the form has already rendered). A dialog's accept button
                 calls this.

A refusal - a wrong password, the sign-in rate limit, a failed Turnstile check - renders in the
form's <Form_Errors />. The host decides how many tries a user gets: count the false results of
submit().

The look is Bootstrap's form classes, so the application's theme applies; restyle with rules
on .Password_Confirmation_Form.
--%>
<Define:Password_Confirmation_Form tag="div">
    <% if (this.data.options === null) { %>
        <div class="Password_Confirmation_Form__loading text-muted">Loading...</div>
    <% } else if (!this.data.options.has_password && !this._passkey_available()) { %>
        <div class="alert alert-warning mb-0">
            This account has no password or passkey that can confirm it is you here.
        </div>
    <% } else { %>
        <p class="Password_Confirmation_Form__intro">
            For your security, confirm it is you before continuing.
        </p>

        <Rsx_Form $sid="form" $controller="Rsx_Password_Confirmation_Controller" $method="verify">
            <Form_Errors />

            <% if (this.data.options.has_password) { %>
                <div class="mb-3">
                    <label class="form-label">Password</label>
                    <Password_Input $sid="password" $name="password" />
                </div>
            <% } %>

            <Turnstile_Input />
        </Rsx_Form>

        <% if (this._passkey_available()) { %>
            <div class="Password_Confirmation_Form__passkey">
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-link px-0" $sid="passkey">
                    <%= this.data.options.has_password ? 'Use a passkey instead' : 'Use a passkey' %>
                </button>
                <div class="text-danger small" $sid="passkey_error"></div>
            </div>
        <% } %>
    <% } %>
</Define:Password_Confirmation_Form>
